                [
                    117.0,
                    378.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Like your readers, you will usually be more motivated by large questions. But limited resources—time, funding, knowledge, skill, pages—may keep you from addressing a large question satisfactorily. So you have to find a question you can answer. When you plan your paper, look for a question that is small enough to answer but is also connected to another question large enough for you and your readers to care about.",
            "block_bbox": [
                114,
                393,
                772,
                513
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 5,
            "global_block_id": 5,
            "global_group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    114.0,
                    393.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    393.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    513.0
                ],
                [
                    114.0,
                    513.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Stating the Solution",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                564,
                330,
                596
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    564.0
                ],
                [
                    330.0,
                    564.0
                ],
                [
                    330.0,
                    596.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    596.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The solution is your main point or claim. We solve practical problems with action: readers (or someone) must change what they do. We solve conceptual problems with information: readers (or someone) must change what they think. Your answer to a small question then helps readers understand a larger one.",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                609,
                772,
                713
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 7,
            "global_block_id": 7,
            "global_group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    78.0,
                    609.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    609.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    713.0
                ],
                [
                    78.0,
                    713.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Practical Problems: What We Should Do To solve a practical problem, you must propose that the reader (or someone) do something to change a condition in the world:",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                724,
                772,
                800
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 8,
            "global_block_id": 8,
            "global_group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
